{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "WMGT Weekly Tournament Report Generator",
  "description": "Generate the Discord-ready weekly recap with verified results, divisions, badges, and player stories",
  "version": "2",
  "when": {
    "type": "userTriggered",
    "patterns": [
      "**/*"
    ]
  },
  "inputs": [
    {
      "name": "week_code",
      "type": "text",
      "label": "Week",
      "placeholder": "e.g., S18W03",
      "required": true,
      "description": "Enter the tournament week code to analyze"
    }
  ],
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "Create the completed, Discord-ready tournament recap for {{week_code}}. Read reports/weekly_tournament_report_workflow.md first, then review reports/S20_reports/S20W01_Tournament_Report.md and reports/S20_reports/S20W02_Tournament_Report.md for the exact presentation style.\n\nConnect to the saved \"wmgt\" database using SQLcl and use only completed results for {{week_code}}. Follow the workflow's required query definitions and validation checklist. In particular, source every display name from wmg_players_v.player_name, never wmg_players.name, and do not add player Discord @ tags.\n\nWrite the final report to reports/<season>_reports/{{week_code}}_Tournament_Report.md, substituting <season> with the season portion of the supplied week code (for example, reports/S21_reports/S21W01_Tournament_Report.md). Create the season directory if it does not exist.\n\nThe report must retain the established recap structure: title, courses, participant/rank-mix line, concise verified narrative, tied podium placements, Amateur/Semi-Pro/Pro divisions, Player(s) of the Week and Hidden gems, new-rank achievements, diamond players, coconuts and system badges, top course scores, and the registration footer. Do not invent achievements or counts; show **None** where a report section has no qualifying results.\n\nFor Player(s) of the Week, exclude overall positions 1-3, calculate each player's improvement as rank average position minus player position, select the highest qualifying improvement (15+ positions), and include every player tied for that top improvement. Use dense ranks for ties in the podium and division standings.\n\nBefore saving, verify the week exists and is completed, all reported player names match query output, all score totals/course codes/badge counts are exact, and the output contains no unresolved placeholders."
  }
}
